Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to fs/ns.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    the mount table of one namespace (kernel heap, one block per
    namespace that differs from its parent's)   at most 4 KiB -> 1 KiB
A table grows as binds are made (the boot namespace is 90 bytes); the limit
only bounds what a program can make the kernel allocate.  1 KiB is about 50
binds.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/fs/ns.ad --label b/fs/ns.ad fs/ns.ad <copy>

--- a/fs/ns.ad
+++ b/fs/ns.ad
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 NS_NOCONN: uint32 = 0xFFFF          # an entry's connection number when its target is not on a 9P server
 
 NS_GROUPS: uint32 = 32              # = the dimension of ns_groups below
-NS_TAB_MAX: uint32 = 4096           # bytes of entries in one table (a board may patch it)
+NS_TAB_MAX: uint32 = 1024           # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 4096
 NS_NAME_MAX: uint32 = 127           # longest from/to path
 NS_LABEL_MAX: uint32 = 31
 NS_HDR: uint32 = 16
